  "text_md": "# Shamanism and Eco-cosmology A cross-cultural perspective\nLagoumitzi and Trikoupi Str., Athens\n## Date: 27 & 28th April 2017\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile2.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile51.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile45.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile28.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile16.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile18.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile38.png>)\nKopenawa, Davi / Bruce Albert 2013.The Falling Sky. Words of a Yanomami Shaman. Harvard University Press.\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile32.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile29.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile15.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile11.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile21.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile47.png>)\nDescola, Philippe 2013 Beyond Nature and Culture. The University of Chicago Press. Original: Descola, Philippe 2005. Par-delà de la nature et culture. Paris: Gallimard.\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile27.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile23.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile41.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile13.png>)\n1\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile22.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile10.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile4.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile44.png>)\nOrganised & Conceptualised by Stefano Beggiora, Ca Foscari University, Venice Diana Riboli, Panteio University, Athens Lidia Guzy, Marginalised & Endangered Worldviews Study Centre, University College Cork, Cork Davide Torri, Heidelberg University, Heidelberg\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile5.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile6.png>)\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile1.png>)\nThis workshop focusses eco-cosmology as a worldview prevalent in shamanic cultures worldwide. Contemporary shamanisms are embedded in analogous ecological knowledge systems relating always to indigenous cosmologies and ontologies (Kopenawa/Albert 2013). Local shamanisms are commonly understood as value systems based on the one hand on cultures of orality, on the other hand on the non-dualistic perspective on human and non-human agencies in a mutually shared world and cosmos (Descola 1992, (2005) 2013, Viveiro de Castro 1998).\n![](<0dd31f954c25db440baccc3245daf51b4b55_page_1_pg1_images/imageFile50.png>)",
